sion `toNodeHandler` already performs internally. Use it to feed `isLegacyRequest()` (or `handler.fetch()`) from a hand-wired Node/Express `(req, res)` handler instead of assembling a `globalThis.Request` from `req.headers` by hand. When a body parser already consumed the Node stream (`express.json()`), pass the parsed value as `parsedBody`; pass `options.signal` to tie the constructed request to client disconnect, the way `toNodeHandler` does.\n./packages/middleware/node/CHANGELOG.md:38:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Add Origin header validation alongside the existing Host header validation. The server package gains framework-agnostic helpers (`validateOriginHeader`, `localhostAllowedOrigins`, `originValidationResponse`); the Express, Hono and Fastify adapters gain `originValidation` /\n./packages/middleware/node/CHANGELOG.md:39:  `localhostOriginValidation` middleware and a new `allowedOrigins` option on their app factories, which now arm Origin validation by default for localhost-class binds (mirroring the Host validation ladder; the 0.0.0.0-without-allowlist warning is unchanged). Requests\n./packages/middleware/node/CHANGELOG.md:40:  without an `Origin` header pass — non-browser MCP clients are unaffected — while a present `Origin` that is not allowed or cannot be parsed (including the opaque `null` origin) is rejected with `403`. The Node adapter ships `hostHeaderValidation` / `originValidation`\n./packages/middleware/node/CHANGELOG.md:41:  request guards for plain `node:http` servers, which previously had no validation helpers.\n./packages/middleware/node/CHANGELOG.md:47:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Forward `setSupportedProtocolVersions` from `NodeStreamableHTTPServerTransport` to the wrapped Web Standard transport. Previously a server's `supportedProtocolVersions` option never reached the Node adapter's `MCP-Protocol-Version` header validation, which silently kept\n./packages/codemod/package.json:4:    \"description\": \"Codemod to migrate MCP TypeScript SDK code from v1 to v2\",\n./packages/codemod/README.md:3:Codemods for migrating MCP TypeScript SDK code between major versions.\n./packages/codemod/README.md:66:CJS→ESM / Node 20 pre-flight, header **read** rewrites (`ctx.http?.req?.headers`\n./packages/codemod/README.md:67:bracket access → `.get()`; sending plain-record headers keeps working), OAuth\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-auth.test.ts:5: * `hosting:context:web-request-headers`, whose bodies hand-host an Express or\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-auth.test.ts:12: * verifies the Authorization header and, on success, hands the verified\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-auth.test.ts:14: * `authInfo` from request headers; it is strictly pass-through to the factory's\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-auth.test.ts:35:/** What the user's verifier derives from the Authorization header (a fresh object per request, so the assertion checks delivery, not identity). */\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-auth.test.ts:36:function verifyBearer(header: string | null): AuthInfo | undefined {\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-auth.test.ts:37:    if (header !== `Bearer ${VALID_TOKEN}`) return undefined;\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-auth.test.ts:52:            headers: {\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-auth.test.ts:76:        const authInfo = verifyBearer(request.headers.get('authorization'));\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-auth.test.ts:81:    // 1. Raw probe without an Authorization header: the gate answers 401 with\n./test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-a