 MCP spec, a server that declares a capability MUST respond to that\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:93:     * JSON Schema validator for elicitation response validation.\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:95:     * The validator is used to validate user input returned from elicitation\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:209:/** Connection-scoped client-identity fields backfilled per request from a validated `_meta` envelope. */\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:219: * per-request server instance from the request's validated `_meta` envelope, so the\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:242: * An MCP server on top of a pluggable transport.\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:286:            sendElicitation: (params, options) => this._sendElicitationLeg(params, options, { validateAcceptedContent: false }),\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:350:                ctx.sessionId || (ctx.http?.req?.headers.get('mcp-session-id') as string) || undefined;\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:446:     * Enforces server-side validation for `tools/call` results regardless of how the\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:452:     * input-required return skips result-schema validation and is checked\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:501:            // Era-exact validation via the function-only WireCodec contract:\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:509:            const validatedRequest = codec.validateRequest('tools/call', request);\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:510:            if (!validatedRequest.ok) {\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:512:                    validatedRequest.reason === 'not-in-era' ? ProtocolErrorCode.InternalError : ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams,\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:513:                    validatedRequest.reason === 'not-in-era'\n./packages/server/src/server/server.ts:515:                        : `Invalid tools/call request: ${validatedRequest.message}`\n./packages/server/