ponse content does not match requested schema: ${validationResult.errorMessage}`\n./packages/middleware/hono/README.md:3:Hono adapters for the MCP TypeScript server SDK.\n./packages/middleware/hono/README.md:7:It does **not** implement MCP itself. Instead, it helps you:\n./packages/middleware/hono/README.md:9:- create a Hono app with sensible defaults for MCP servers\n./packages/middleware/hono/README.md:11:- add DNS rebinding protection via Host header validation (recommended for localhost servers)\n./packages/middleware/hono/README.md:41:### Host header validation (DNS rebinding protection)\n./packages/server/src/server/completable.ts:21: * Wraps a schema to provide autocompletion capabilities. Useful for, e.g., prompt arguments in MCP.\n./test/integration/test/issues/test_1342OauthErrorHttp200.test.ts:6: * with a confusing Zod validation error. This test verifies that the SDK properly\n./packages/client/src/client/authErrors.ts:57: * Thrown when an authorization-server issuer identifier fails validation.\n./packages/client/src/client/authErrors.ts:64: *   callback failed RFC 9207 §2.4 validation against the recorded issuer.\n./packages/client/src/client/authErrors.ts:82:    /** The issuer the client expected (from validated metadata / discovery input). */\n./packages/client/src/client/authErrors.ts:109: * not a recoverable-by-credential-invalidation condition, and staying outside\n./packages/client/src/client/authErrors.ts:163: * step-up (e.g. a minimal `AuthProvider`, `requestInit`-only headers, or no\n./packages/client/src/client/authErrors.ts:173: * All fields originate from the resource server's `WWW-Authenticate` header;\n./packages/server/src/server/perRequestTransport.ts:20: * the protocol layer validates it against the serving instance's negotiated\n./packages/server/src/server/perRequestTransport.ts:22: * inbound request's headers here.\n./packages/server/src/server/perRequestTransport.ts:25: * transport: session ids and session headers, resumability (ev